“We think this bill is one of the most impactful things we could be doing in education now,” said Jessica Handy, the executive director of Stand for Children Illinois. “Kids lose a significant amount of instructional time because of time on their phones. It’s such a barrier to students being able to focus.”

Our schools are almost phone-free! Recently, SB2427, limiting student phone use during instructional time, passed the House and moved on to the Senate. This bill will restore about one hour more learning time to students, improve students’ educational and social experience in school, and become the most equitable cell phone policy in the country.

